=== 5. what is proved and what is not ===
   PROVED : if sum_j j m_j 2^{-j} x^{j-1} converges at some x > 1, then Gamma^(q) has no
            zero in a disc about q = 1/2 whose radius depends only on that series and on
            Gamma(A) >= 3 -- uniformly in k.  The fair coin is never pinched there.
   NOT    : the converse.  A radius of convergence equal to 1 removes the obstruction to
            a zero near q = 1/2; it does not produce one.  The lacunary family is pinched,
            and that is one family.
